file: "packages/editor/src/shell/app.tsx"
doc: "The editor shell: islands, overlays, load and save wiring."

constants: [
  { name: "App"
    change_type: MODIFIED
    doc:
      "One change, to the local `mode` accessor that feeds StateIsland's\n"
      "`mode` prop. Everything else -- the islands, both overlays, loading,\n"
      "saving, the error effect -- is untouched.\n"
      "\n"
      "`mode` today returns the active tool's label when the tool is not\n"
      "'select', and undefined otherwise. It gains a branch AHEAD of that\n"
      "one: when ui.modalGesture() is defined, return a string describing the\n"
      "gesture instead.\n"
      "\n"
      "The gesture wins over the tool because a modal gesture is the more\n"
      "transient of the two and is the one the next keystroke acts on. A\n"
      "user in grab mode with the hand tool active needs to be told they are\n"
      "in grab mode.\n"
      "\n"
      "The string is built here rather than in StateIsland, which takes a\n"
      "plain string and formats nothing. Its two parts:\n"
      "  the word 'Grab' for kind 'grab', 'Resize' for kind 'resize'\n"
      "  then, when `digits` is not the empty string, a space and the digits\n"
      "So an untouched grab reads 'Grab' and typing 4 then 0 makes it read\n"
      "'Grab 40'. The direction is not named: the preview already shows it,\n"
      "and a mode line that restates what is drawn under it is noise.\n"
      "\n"
      "Echoing the digits is not decoration. Typing a digit is the one\n"
      "keystroke in the gesture that changes nothing else on screen: the\n"
      "preview and the dimming both come from modalDelta, which is the zero\n"
      "vector until an arrow has aimed the gesture, so 4 then 0 before any\n"
      "arrow moves no outline. The mode line is the only place those two\n"
      "keystrokes are visible.\n"
      "\n"
      "This is a claim about the DIGIT keystrokes specifically, not about\n"
      "the gesture. Opening one already changes the screen -- the targets\n"
      "dim and draw a preview outline in place, before any key is typed.\n"
      "\n"
      "StateIslandProps needs no change. Its doc field already records that\n"
      "`mode` is 'a short human string, not an enum' and that 'editor-shell\n"
      "v2b feeds it the modal g/r gesture from UiState instead' -- this is\n"
      "that caller change."
    type: { unsupported: { reason: RAW_EXPRESSION, source_excerpt: "Component<{}>" } }
    uses: ["ModalGesture"]
  }
]
